      "message": "Yes. As I described in IssueTracker. \nhttps://issuetracker.google.com/issues/236300341\n\nFor example:\n\nIf we only assign value to bri-\u003escl_gpiod without assigning value to bri-\u003erecover_bus in I2C Adapter, this will cause i2c_recover_bus to not work.\nSo I think this check is useful. \n\nAs I said in IssueTracker the value of bri-\u003erecover_bus comes from I2C Adapter. If CONFIG_CFI_CLANG is enabled and this check is retained causes bri-\u003eset_scl to be empty. Because bri-\u003eset_scl is empty, dump happens here:\nhttps://android.googlesource.com/kernel/common/+/refs/heads/android13-5.15/drivers/i2c/i2c-core-base.c#217 \n\nAccording to my understanding, this check cannot take effect after enabling CONFIG_CFI_CLANG.\n\nSorry for replying late.",
